{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>You shall not wear sha'atnez, wool and linen together.</b> Woven or sewn one with the other — this is 'together' (יחדו). But it is permitted to wear a garment of wool over a garment of linen, for this is not יחדו; and hides of wool may be sewn with linen threads, since they are not a garment. And the secret of this commandment I have already written in the section on kedoshim."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:15.416879207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}